---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Split from '../components/Split.astro'
import MomentsSection from '../components/MomentsSection.astro'
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro'
import { imageByFilename } from '../data/homePageImages'

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL

const planVisitMomentsItems = [
  {
    image: imageByFilename('489054059_18163289533338056_8029010570585607191_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'People gathered together during worship at Pine Lake',
  },
  {
    image: imageByFilename('649217566_18197705956338056_8287619439099906475_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'A church service moment at Pine Lake',
  },
  {
    image: imageByFilename('659595691_18200889961338056_2843340499663516152_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'Kids and families connecting in community',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Plan a Visit | Pine Lake Covenant Church"
  description="What to expect on Sundays at Pine Lake, including location, service format, and family details."
>
  <div class="canvas">
    <Split
      class="to-full"
      filename="651034879_18198219322338056_9008954644945760140_n.jpg"
      alt="A volunteer making coffee at the welcome café before the service"
      tone="sand"
      reverse
      eyebrow="Plan a Visit"
    >
      <h1 class="display">Plan a Visit</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Visiting a church for the first time can feel awkward — especially if you haven’t been to one in a while (or
        ever). Our hope is simple: that you’d feel comfortable, unpressured, and free to participate at whatever level
        feels right to you.
      </p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">When &amp; where</p>
      <h2>Sundays at 10:00am</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        1715 228th Ave SE, Sammamish, WA 98075. There’s plenty of guest parking available, including accessible parking
        near the main entrance.
      </p>

      <figure class="media">
        <Photo
          filename="church-exterior-1024x400.jpg"
          alt="Pine Lake Covenant Church building in Sammamish"
          class="media__img media__img--cover"
        />
        <figcaption class="media__caption">
          Our building in Sammamish — look for guest parking near the main entrance.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <Split
      class="to-full"
      filename="719135962_18207937108338056_3061581680291060435_n.jpg"
      alt="The congregation standing in worship on a Sunday morning"
      tone="paper"
      eyebrow="The morning"
      heading="What happens on a Sunday"
    >
      <p>
        Our services last about <strong>75 minutes</strong> and include a mix of music, teaching, and time together.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Around <strong>20 minutes of contemporary worship music</strong>, led by a band — join in, or just listen
        </li>
        <li>A short kids’ moment and a few brief Bible readings</li>
        <li>A brief meet-and-greet to say hello — no pressure; many people simply smile and stay seated</li>
        <li>A <strong>20–25 minute message</strong> that’s thoughtful, practical, and grounded in the Bible</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Once a month, we also share <strong>communion</strong> together. You’re always free to participate — or not — as you
        feel comfortable.
      </p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section section-callout">
      <h2>Will I stand out or be put on the spot?</h2>
      <p>No.</p>
      <p>
        You won’t be asked to introduce yourself, stand up, or share anything publicly. You’re free to come, observe,
        participate as much or as little as you like, and head out when the service ends. Coffee is served, conversation
        is optional, and pressure is not part of the experience.
      </p>
    </section>

    <Split
      class="to-full"
      filename="658026969_18200890024338056_5693344916949832542_n.jpg"
      alt="A child happily playing in the Pine Lake Kids room"
      tone="sand"
      eyebrow="Bringing kids?"
      heading="We make Sundays smooth for parents"
    >
      <ul>
        <li>Programs for children and youth of all ages, from <strong>0–18</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Quick check-in</strong> in the foyer</li>
        <li>All volunteers are <strong>background checked</strong></li>
        <li>A <strong>secure pickup system</strong> for children</li>
        <li>At least <strong>two adults</strong> in every room</li>
        <li>One Sunday a month, <strong>K–5 students stay in the service</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        For babies and toddlers, there’s a comfortable space where you can
        <strong>watch the service while caring for your child</strong>. You can learn more on our
        <a href={`${base}families/kids/`}>Kids &amp; Families</a> page.
      </p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">A few practical things</p>
      <h2>What should I wear?</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        Whatever you’re comfortable in. On any given Sunday you’ll see everything from
        <strong>Seahawks jerseys and jeans</strong> to <strong>smart casual</strong>. There’s no dress code, and no
        expectations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MomentsSection heading={null} items={planVisitMomentsItems} sectionClass="to-wide" />

    <section class="band band--forest to-full visit-cta">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">No test required</p>
        <h2>A place to belong</h2>
        <p>
          Some people who come to Pine Lake are deeply rooted in their faith. Others are exploring, returning after time
          away, or connected through family or community. All are welcome — you’ll never be asked what you believe to be
          welcome here.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you’d like to connect with someone ahead of time, you’re always welcome to —
          <a href={`${base}contact/`}>say hello</a> — but there’s no expectation that you do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .visit-cta .band__inner {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .visit-cta h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .visit-cta a {
    color: var(--color-white);
    text-decoration-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }
</style>
